sec 7.4: the retiring seq is taken over byte strings that pass sec 4.3; bytes that spell a succession of the root at seq 1 and fail sec 4.3, anchored by the root in the second of its handing off, leave the retiring seq at 2: the succession at 2 is timely, the record over the failing bytes is one at which the root has not retired, it counts, its hash is MISSING and the bytes MALFORMED.
